WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.302
-Dozens of prominent
New York Democrats,

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.872
from Chuck Schumer
to Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez,

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.306
have called
on Governor Andrew Cuomo

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:10.376
to resign after a flood
of sexual harassment allegations

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:12.378
and the revelation
that his administration

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.814
covered up the COVID death toll
in nursing homes.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.150
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.154
♪♪

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.355
New York Governor Andrew Cuomo

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.490
has had such a precipitous fall
from grace that,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.192
in the span
of just a few months,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.961
he's gone from winning an Emmy;
writing a best-selling book;

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:32.064 line:0%
and doing prop comedy
with giant medical swabs on CNN,

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:35.268 line:0%
like a dental hygienist
at a middle school assembly,

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.203 line:0%
to facing calls
for his resignation

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.505 line:0%
from dozens
of his fellow Democrats,

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:42.408 line:0%
including some of New York's
most prominent lawmakers.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.844 line:0%
-The majority of House Democrats
from New York

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.146 line:0%
are calling for Cuomo's
resignation,

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:50.850 line:0%
including Representative
Alexandra Ocasio-Cortez.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.020 line:0%
Chairman of the House Committee
on the Judiciary Jerry Nadler

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.855 line:0%
released a statement saying...

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:07.900 line:0%
-More than 50 state Democratic
lawmakers, legislators,

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.002 line:0%
signed onto a letter yesterday,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.103 line:0%
also calling on Cuomo
to resign.

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.339 line:0%
-It's clear that Governor Cuomo

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.241 line:0%
has lost the confidence

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.942 line:0%
of his governing partners,

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:18.778 line:0%
as well as the people
of New York.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.746 line:0%
-It is disgusting to me

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.982 line:0%
and he can no longer serve
as governor.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.150 line:0%
-It's clear to me
that the governor

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.651 line:0%
can no longer be effective.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:27.920 line:0%
-Governor Cuomo has lost
the confidence

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.189 line:0%
of his governing partners

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.990 line:0%
and of so many New Yorkers.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.693 line:0%
So, for the good of the state,
he should resign.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.294
-First of all, you know
you're in a bad spot

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:37.630
when even Chuck Schumer calls
on you to resign.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.498
That dude doesn't do
anything hastily.

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:40.867
Before he makes any decision,

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.102
he has to have at least
four brow furrows

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.537
and inch his glasses
down to the tip of his nose.

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:48.374
Chuck Schumer makes decisions
so slowly that, one time,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.176
he was ordering
at an Italian restaurant

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.544
and the waiter
stood there so long,

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.412
he died of exposure.

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.381
[ As Schumer ]
Let's see.
Rigatoni? No.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.582
Ziti?
Too heavy.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.651
Do you have any --
Aah!

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.220
Second, so many Democrats have
called on Cuomo to resign that,

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.089
at this point it's easier
to ask who hasn't done so.

00:02:04.089 --> 00:02:06.092
Good news, Governor --
the Oswego County commissioner

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:08.661
for Water and Sewer Service
is standing by us -- Wait.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.563
Nope, sorry.
He said you should resign.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.397
Somebody call the
Schenectady Parks Department!

00:02:12.397 --> 00:02:13.966
They'll never turn on us!

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:15.735
And, just to give you
a visual representation

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.437
of the dramatic collapse
of Cuomo's political standing,

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:19.772
here he is in November,

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.941
accepting an Emmy
for his COVID briefings;

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.510
and here he is on Friday,
at the governor's mansion,

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.247
wrapped in a blanket,
holding a bottle of something.

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.581
[ As Cuomo ]
Nobody panic.
We're going to be fine.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.115
Now, get me
my thinking blanket.

00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:31.583
I need to make some calls.

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.786
It's never good when your
governor starts dressing like

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.822
Nicole Kidman's therapist
from some HBO murder show.

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:38.057
Looks like someone's
deadbeat dad,

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.591
who hangs around beach bonfires

00:02:39.591 --> 00:02:42.161
and tries to start sing-alongs
to "Brown Eyed Girl."

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.896
I'm not saying his
administration is a shipwreck,

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:46.131
but that's how guys dressed
when they tried

00:02:46.131 --> 00:02:48.434
to sneak
onto a Titanic lifeboat.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.136
[ Falsetto ]
Am I a man?
Oh, gracious, no.

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:53.239
My name is
Mrs., uh, Bottle Blanket.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:56.142
And, yet, Cuomo has, so far,
resisted the pressure to resign,

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.576
blaming it on council culture

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.579
and insisting
that he's being targeted

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:02.148
because he's not part
of the political establishment.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.516 line:0%
-People know the difference

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:07.486 line:0%
between playing politics,

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:09.522 line:0%
bowing to cancel culture,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:12.225 line:0%
and the truth.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.960 line:0%
Let the review proceed.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.662 line:0%
I'm not going to resign.

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:19.098 line:0%
I was not elected
by the politicians.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.467 line:0%
I was elected by the people.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:26.139 line:0%
Part of this is that I am not
part of the political club.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.707
-Alright, first of all,
can we now agree

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.142
that the term cancel culture
is officially meaningless?

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:32.411
He's using the same line
as the people who spent

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.480
the last three weeks
getting mad about the Muppets,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.215
Mr. Potato Head,
and Looney Tunes.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:38.584
[ As Cuomo ]
This is just like
what happened to Dr. Seuss.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:39.652
The only difference is

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.054
I do run the zoo.

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:44.824
Second, how can you say you're
not part of the political club?

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:46.492
You're the son
of a former governor,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.027
you were
in Bill Clinton's Cabinet,

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.063
your last name is on a bridge.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:53.365
That's like Al Unser Jr. saying
he didn't come from car people.

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:54.634
It really can't be understated,

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.936
just how dramatic a downfall
this has been for Cuomo.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.104
It wasn't long ago, of course,

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.939
that he was winning
national acclaim

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.241
for his performances
of coronaviruses briefings,

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:03.809
where he, among other things,

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:06.078
displayed his mastery
of the calendar.

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:07.346
-Today is Saturday.

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:08.347
That is a fact.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:09.615
Today is Sunday.

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:10.716
Today is Friday.

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:11.850
Today is Saturday.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:12.985
Today's Monday.

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:14.320
Today is Thursday.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.721
Today is Saturday.

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:17.756
-I mean, it really
gives you an idea

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:19.359
of just how surreal
and horrifying

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.826
the early days
of the pandemic were,

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.294
that we all found it soothing

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:24.663
to watch a guy with all
the charm and charisma

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:26.532
of an outer borough
mattress salesman

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.733
tell us what day
of the week it was.

00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:29.935
If Andrew Cuomo's dad
hadn't been governor,

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.237
there's a good chance
he'd be working

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.272
at one of those used car
dealerships in Queens

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.975
that does local ads
during Yankee broadcasts.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.510
[ As Cuomo ]
Come on down to Cuomo Kiev,
Kew Gardens.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.913
Cuomo cars, Cuomo savings.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.081
Isn't that right,

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:44.550
former Yankees
third baseman Scott Brosius?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.618
Today is Monday.

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.520
Now, that's a home run.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.422
Again, I get why we
found them reassuring.

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:52.291
I did, too.
I did, too.

00:04:52.291 --> 00:04:54.260
It was a scary time
and there was a leadership void

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.595
and he stepped into it.
There were times

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:58.197
when I genuinely
did not know what day it was.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.798
It's not like I was
grabbing a newspaper

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:01.200
on my daily commute
to the attic.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.736
The same controlling
authoritarian tendencies

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.338
Cuomo has displayed
throughout his career

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:06.839
also made him
a commanding presence

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.440
when everyone
was desperate for one.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.777
And, as a result, he turned
himself into a TV star,

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.711
he won an Emmy,
wrote a best-selling book,

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:14.981
stirred speculation
that he might run for president

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.782
or become Joe Biden's
attorney general,

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:19.852
and earned a nickname that was
super cringey at the time

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.754
and, in retrospect,
so much worse.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.155 line:0%
-The governor of New York,

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:24.556 line:0%
Andrew Cuomo, he has been

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:25.557 line:0%
front and center, right?

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:26.926 line:0%
During this pandemic,

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.495 line:0%
holding coronavirus briefings
during the week,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.831 line:0%
talking to, updating,
the country.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.632 line:0%
Lately, he has been asked
by many,

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:36.669 line:0%
including his own brother,
CNN's Chris Cuomo,

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.204 line:0%
if he will run for president.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:39.905 line:0%
-We are learning
that Governor Cuomo

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:40.906 line:0%
may be in the running

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:42.541 line:0%
for Joe Biden's
attorney general.

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:43.909 line:0%
-[ Laughing ]
-The Luv Guv,

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:47.279 line:0%
here on "GMA"
this Monday morning.

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:48.814 line:0%
-The Luv Guv?

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:51.550 line:0%
-Yeah, that's
Andrew Cuomo's nickname.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.918 line:0%
You didn't know that?
-Now, you know,

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:54.887 line:0%
I've seen you referred to
a little bit recently

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.055 line:0%
as the Luv Guv.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.491 line:0%
-The New York Post dubbed you
the new Luv Guv.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.427
-Ugh! No politician should ever
be called the Luv Guv.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.663
That sounds like the name
of an early 2000s bro comedy

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:06.666
starring Owen Wilson
as a college dropout

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:08.166
who accidentally
becomes governor.

00:06:08.166 --> 00:06:10.369
[ As Wilson ]
Oh, man, I got to clean my room

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:12.605
before the legislature
comes over.

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:13.739
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:15.374
And, now, all that acclaim
has vaporized

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.608
nearly overnight,

00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:18.110
as the real Andrew Cuomo
has caught up

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.112
to the character
Andrew Cuomo was playing on TV,

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:21.581
or, as The New Republic
put it...

00:06:26.218 --> 00:06:27.353
And the newspaper character
is always

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.255
so much worse
than the TV character.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.123
In the newspaper,
those "Fireside" cartoons

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.858
are just a bunch
of dumb cavemen,

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:34.093
but in the TV show,
they were played

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:36.428
by Ryan Gosling
and Timothée Chalamet.

00:06:36.428 --> 00:06:38.063
The point is,
Cuomo's TV audience

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:40.532
is now learning
about the real Andrew Cuomo,

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:43.702
as he faces accusations
of bullying and abuse of power,

00:06:43.702 --> 00:06:46.439
creating a toxic workplace
environment, a COVID cover-up,

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:48.574
and allegations
of sexual harassment

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.675
from at least six women.

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:52.077 line:0%
-Over the last two weeks,
six women,

00:06:52.077 --> 00:06:55.181 line:0%
including current and former
members of Cuomo's staff,

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.249 line:0%
have accused him
of sexual harassment

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:59.251 line:0%
and unwanted advances.

00:06:59.251 --> 00:07:01.920 line:0%
-The allegations against Cuomo
range from allegations

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.089 line:0%
of inappropriate touching

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:06.825 line:0%
and inquiries about the sex
lives of his subordinates

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:09.094 line:0%
to allegations
of unwanted kissing

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:11.264 line:0%
and a request
to play strip poker

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:12.965 line:0%
during a trip
on a government plane.

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.500
-Ugh! Why is strip poker
the spin the bottle

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.535
of gross, older dudes?

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:17.670
Also, what's the appeal?

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.472
Like I don't have a good body,

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.640
but the worst
it's going to look is naked

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.342
and hunched over a card table.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:24.410
Plus, it's extra bad for me

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.478
because my tell,
when I'm bluffing, is

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:27.613
my penis gets smaller.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:29.882
That's what happened, everyone!

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.050
I don't know what to tell you!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.085
I was bluffing!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:36.288
Let's let it go
and deal the cards!

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:37.990
Apparently, another one
of Cuomo's tactics was

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.192
to ask female aides
for tech help.

00:07:40.192 --> 00:07:41.561
One former aide said Cuomo...

00:07:47.066 --> 00:07:48.167
And then...

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.249
Nothing says "sexy" like,

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:05.318
"I'm too old
to figure out my phone."

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:06.485
What a horrible pickup line.

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:07.786
That's like saying,
"Hey, babe, got a minute?

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:10.389
My VCR keeps blinking 12:00."

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:12.424
Also, I'm sorry, you couldn't
find your notes app?

00:08:12.424 --> 00:08:13.926
It's right there.
It's on the home screen.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.728
Looks like a notepad
that says "Notes."

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:17.395
How many more clues do you need?

00:08:17.395 --> 00:08:19.432
[ As Cuomo ]
How do I access it?
Do I yell at it?

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:21.033
Notes, open!

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:22.034
Begin note.

00:08:22.034 --> 00:08:23.936
Today is Monday.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:26.138
And, in addition to the sexual
harassment allegations,

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.107
Cuomo's also dealing
with the fallout

00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:30.076
from his administration's
alleged cover-up

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:31.944
of coronavirus deaths
in nursing homes.

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:34.680
Cuomo and his administration
are facing investigations

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.348
from the FBI and U.S. attorney

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:39.151
and an impeachment inquiry
from the state legislature,

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:42.020
after the state attorney general
found that his administration

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.990
had severely undercounted
COVID deaths in nursing homes.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.625
-The New York Times
reporting tonight,

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:48.994
top aides to New York's
Governor Andrew Cuomo

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:52.731 line:0%
rewrote a report
in summer of last year

00:08:52.731 --> 00:08:55.267 line:0%
to hide the number
of nursing home deaths

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:57.169 line:0%
due to the coronavirus.

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:59.238 line:0%
In the wake of Cuomo

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:02.341 line:0%
ordering nursing homes
to take in all individuals,

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:04.109 line:0%
even with COVID, in March 2020,

00:09:04.109 --> 00:09:06.612 line:0%
which, critics say,
led to loss of life,

00:09:06.612 --> 00:09:10.449 line:0%
some of Cuomo's top aides
allegedly rewrote

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:12.484 line:0%
a June 2020 nursing home report

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:15.854 line:0%
to hide the high COVID
death toll in nursing homes,

00:09:15.854 --> 00:09:17.589 line:0%
cutting it by nearly half.

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:19.291
-That's right,
they just rewrote the report,

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:21.259
they covered it up, they lied,
and, if they lied

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:22.962
about the COVID death toll
in nursing homes,

00:09:22.962 --> 00:09:25.331
you have to ask yourself, "What
else are they lying about?"

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:27.099
Wait a second.
Today isn't Saturday!

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:30.202
It's Thursday!
And, look, again, I get why.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:33.339
To anyone who watched Cuomo
on TV during the pandemic,

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:34.973
this might all be
a little bit shocking,

00:09:34.973 --> 00:09:36.142
but to people
who have chronicled

00:09:36.142 --> 00:09:37.910
his career in New York,
it's anything but.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.645
For one thing,
Cuomo has long been a nemesis

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:42.682
to progressives in the state,
often siding with Republicans,

00:09:42.682 --> 00:09:44.983
and even helping them maintain
control of the state Senate.

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:47.119 line:0%
For years,
he threatened to destroy

00:09:47.119 --> 00:09:49.455 line:0%
Democratic member
of the state assembly Ron Kim,

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:51.757 line:0%
for criticizing his handling
of nursing homes.

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:53.025
And, last year, at the same time

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:54.993
that he was winning plaudits
for his COVID briefings,

00:09:54.993 --> 00:09:57.562
he was also proposing
massive cuts to Medicaid,

00:09:57.562 --> 00:09:59.832
which included $400 million
in cuts to hospitals --

00:09:59.832 --> 00:10:01.033
in the middle of a pandemic.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:02.968
That's like showing up
to a burning building

00:10:02.968 --> 00:10:04.302
with that month's water bill.

00:10:04.302 --> 00:10:06.805
[ As Cuomo ]
Oof! This is going to be
a hefty one.

00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:09.275
Cuomo also saw an exodus
of public health officials

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:10.676
from his administration,
after he...

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:14.513
...according
to The New York Times,

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:16.782
seizing control of the state's
vaccination program,

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:19.184
sidelining experts,
and ignoring their advice.

00:10:19.184 --> 00:10:22.187
And Cuomo even went so far
as to make this stunning remark.

00:10:22.187 --> 00:10:28.159
-When I say, "experts,"
in air quotes,

00:10:28.159 --> 00:10:29.828
it sounds like I'm saying

00:10:29.828 --> 00:10:33.833
I don't really trust
the "experts."

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:35.767
Because I don't.

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:37.402
Because I don't.

00:10:37.402 --> 00:10:39.504
-That's some real sports radio
call-in energy.

00:10:39.504 --> 00:10:41.307
[ As Cuomo ]
Jets are going all the way
next year.

00:10:41.307 --> 00:10:43.675
Don't trust the experts.
I bet my house on it.

00:10:43.675 --> 00:10:44.810
Okay, it's in my wife's name.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.812
I live in it.
I live in it.

00:10:46.812 --> 00:10:49.215
Also, really, you think you know
better than the experts?

00:10:49.215 --> 00:10:52.218
Okay,
Mr. I Can't Find My Notes App.

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:53.719
Cuomo's long been known
in New York

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.687
as a micromanaging bully
who intimidates

00:10:55.687 --> 00:10:57.223
and coerces people
to get his way,

00:10:57.223 --> 00:10:59.992
which is why he has
so few friends left, now,

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.628
as he faces a stampede
of intensifying scandals.

00:11:02.628 --> 00:11:04.063
And there have been,
in recent days,

00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:05.797
a series of damning exposes

00:11:05.797 --> 00:11:08.000
about the toxic culture
of intimidation

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.402
and imperiousness
he has fostered around him.

00:11:10.402 --> 00:11:11.470
One of those articles,

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.605
by New York Magazine's
Rebecca Traister,

00:11:13.605 --> 00:11:15.975
contains this deeply
revealing anecdote

00:11:15.975 --> 00:11:18.544
about a party at the governor's
mansion a few years ago...

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.426
And, yeah, it is.
Can you imagine that happening

00:11:34.426 --> 00:11:36.529
in any other workplace,
a senior manager joking

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:37.763
about not knowing anyone's name?

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:39.431
Can you imagine if my team
threw up a photo

00:11:39.431 --> 00:11:42.201
of our band leader
and I didn't know his name?

00:11:42.201 --> 00:11:44.336
Ted Ardison?

00:11:44.336 --> 00:11:46.872
[ Laughter ]
Frud Armissing.

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:49.441
The most embarrassing thing
I've ever done at a staff party

00:11:49.441 --> 00:11:50.842
is try to get
everyone's attention

00:11:50.842 --> 00:11:53.813
for an inspirational speech
by tapping a glass with a spoon,

00:11:53.813 --> 00:11:55.380
breaking the glass,
and cutting my finger,

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.982
passing out
when I saw the blood,

00:11:56.982 --> 00:11:58.917
and only waking up when Wally

00:11:58.917 --> 00:12:00.819
threw an entire bucket
of water on me,

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:02.855
which, to this day,
seems like overkill.

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:04.623
Would you agree,
in hindsight, Wally,

00:12:04.623 --> 00:12:07.993
that a bucket
was too much water?!

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:10.996
Okay, great.
Thank you, Wally.

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:12.464
And there have even been
public instances

00:12:12.464 --> 00:12:14.633
of Cuomo brushing off questions
from journalists

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:17.102
about the rampant culture
of sexual harassment in Albany,

00:12:17.102 --> 00:12:19.838
like this heated exchange
with reporters from 2017,

00:12:19.838 --> 00:12:22.140
in which he tried to turn
the question back on them.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.475 line:0%
-You did have it going on

00:12:23.475 --> 00:12:24.976 line:0%
within your own administration,

00:12:24.976 --> 00:12:26.678 line:0%
allegedly, with Sam Hoyt.

00:12:26.678 --> 00:12:27.946 line:0%
What could you do differently

00:12:27.946 --> 00:12:29.848 line:0%
to, you know,
kind of pick up on that?

00:12:29.848 --> 00:12:31.516 line:0%
-Well, look, you have it
going on in journalism.

00:12:31.516 --> 00:12:33.952 line:0%
-Yeah, I know. So --
-What are you going
to do differently?

00:12:33.952 --> 00:12:35.253 line:0%
-But the question's
about state government.

00:12:35.253 --> 00:12:37.155 line:0%
It's not about journalism.
-I could tell you later,

00:12:37.155 --> 00:12:38.457 line:0%
in great detail, about that...
-No.

00:12:38.457 --> 00:12:40.092 line:0%
-if you're interested.
-It's about you

00:12:40.092 --> 00:12:42.361 line:0%
and journalism

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:44.429 line:0%
and it's about you in journalism

00:12:44.429 --> 00:12:46.331 line:0%
and it's about state government

00:12:46.331 --> 00:12:48.600 line:0%
and it's about carpentry.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:49.768
-You can't just
deflect questions

00:12:49.768 --> 00:12:51.236
about sexual harassment
by listing off

00:12:51.236 --> 00:12:52.771
a bunch of random professions.

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:54.139
[ As Cuomo ]
It's about carpentry.

00:12:54.139 --> 00:12:55.607
It's about trucking.

00:12:55.607 --> 00:12:56.942
It's about scuba diving,

00:12:56.942 --> 00:12:58.910
flamenco dancing, beekeeping.

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:00.412
You guys ever wonder

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:02.280
what they're wearing
under those suits?

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.716
Dozens of the most prominent
Democrats in New York

00:13:04.716 --> 00:13:06.185
have called on Cuomo to resign.

00:13:06.185 --> 00:13:07.786
It's a stunning fall from grace.

00:13:07.786 --> 00:13:09.855
People familiar with the TV
version of Andrew Cuomo

00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:11.423
are now meeting
the real Andrew Cuomo.

00:13:11.423 --> 00:13:13.392
Who knows, at this point,
if we'll even make it

00:13:13.392 --> 00:13:14.693
to the end of the week,
given that...

00:13:14.693 --> 00:13:16.095
-Today's Monday.

00:13:16.095 --> 00:13:17.763
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:21.299
♪♪

